# Rock: a straight-eighths rock band at ~120. Drums from the Groove MIDI Dataset (drummer 7, a rock groove
# at 120, CC BY 4.0: styles/README.md), the rest written for Polly over C M7.
# Main A: palm-muted power chords in eighths, a root-eighths bass, the drummer's hi-hat groove.
# Main B: the power chords ring open, an overdriven guitar arpeggio on top, a rock organ underneath,
# a busier kick, the bass climbing to the octave; a crash on its one.
style Rock
tempo 120

track d1 type=bypass chan=10 vol=106 rev=24
track d2 type=bypass chan=10 vol=106 rev=24   # shares channel 10 with d1: the same mixer
track pc type=bypass chan=10 vol=106 rev=24
track ba type=bass program=34 chan=2 lo=E1 hi=G3 hikey=F# vol=108 rev=8
# power chords (root, fifth, octave) low: the high key keeps G..B below C
track c1 type=chord1 program=30 chan=3 lo=E2 hi=G4 hikey=F# vol=78 pan=40 rev=20
track c2 type=chord1 program=29 chan=4 lo=G4 hi=E6 hikey=F# vol=62 pan=88 rev=40
track c3 type=chord2 program=18 chan=5 lo=G3 hi=C5 vol=58 pan=64 rev=40 cho=30

